CAT = "s24Trading"; SEG = "TRD"
Q = [
('A firm routes customer orders to other venues without checking each order separately. Rule 5310 requires it to review execution quality regularly and rigorously at least:',
 'Quarterly, by security and by type of order', ['Once a year, for all securities and order types together', 'Monthly, for customer limit orders only', 'Only when a customer complains about a fill'],
 'Rule 5310.09 requires a firm that does not review each order individually to conduct regular and rigorous reviews of execution quality at least quarterly, on a security-by-security and type-of-order basis.'),
('Under Rule 5310.01, when a member receives a marketable customer order it must:',
 'Make every effort to execute it fully and promptly', ['Hold it until the end of the day for a better price', 'Route it to the exchange that pays the most rebate', 'Ask the customer to resubmit it as a limit order'],
 'Rule 5310.01 requires a member to make every effort to execute a marketable customer order that it receives fully and promptly.'),
("A firm sends a customer's order through a third-party dealer instead of directly to the best available market, making the customer's price worse. This is called:",
 'Interpositioning', ['Front running', 'Marking the close', 'Free-riding'],
 'Rule 5310(b) forbids interjecting a third party between the member and the best market for the security in a way that makes the price to the customer less favorable than under prevailing market conditions.'),
('Rule 611 of Regulation NMS requires trading centers to have policies reasonably designed to prevent:',
 'Trade-throughs of protected quotations', ['Short sales below the last reported sale price', 'Quotes in increments of a penny or more', 'Trading after 4 p.m. Eastern time'],
 'The Order Protection Rule requires policies and procedures reasonably designed to prevent executions at prices inferior to protected quotations displayed by other trading centers, subject to exceptions.'),
("An intermarket sweep order lets a trading center execute at a price that would otherwise trade through another venue's protected quote because:",
 'Orders went out at once to take the better protected quotes', ['The customer agreed in advance to accept a worse price', 'The trade is reported late as an out-of-sequence trade', "The other venue's quote was not firm at the time of the trade"],
 'Under Regulation NMS an intermarket sweep order is a limit order routed while simultaneous orders are sent to take out any better-priced protected quotations, which is an exception to Rule 611.'),
("Under SEC Rule 606, a broker-dealer must publish quarterly reports on where it routes customers' held orders within:",
 'One month after the quarter ends', ['Five business days after the quarter ends', 'Six months after the quarter ends', 'Ten days after each trading day'],
 'Rule 606(a) requires a broker-dealer to make public a quarterly report on its routing of held orders in NMS securities within one month after the end of each calendar quarter, including payment for order flow received.'),
("A market maker holds a customer's limit order to buy at $20.10 and then buys for its own account at $20.08. Under Rule 5320 the firm must:",
 "Fill the customer's order at the same or better price", ["Cancel the customer's order and notify him that day", 'Report the trade to FINRA as a correction', 'Do nothing, since the customer order was not marketable'],
 'Rule 5320 prohibits trading ahead of a customer order: a member that trades for its own account at a price that would satisfy a held customer order must immediately execute the customer order at the same or better price.'),
('A trader learns that a customer is about to place a 50,000-share block order and buys the stock for the firm first. This is:',
 'Front running', ['Spoofing', 'Interpositioning', 'A wash sale'],
 'Rule 5270 prohibits trading in a security or related derivative while in possession of material, non-public market information about an imminent block transaction in that security.'),
('Under Rule 5280, before its research department publishes a new rating, a firm may not:',
 'Adjust its inventory based on knowing about that report', ['Let its traders see any public news about the company', 'Execute unsolicited customer orders in the stock', 'Make markets in any other stocks that its analysts cover'],
 'Rule 5280 forbids a member from establishing, increasing, decreasing or liquidating an inventory position in a security based on non-public advance knowledge of a research report, and requires information barriers.'),
('Under Regulation SHO Rule 203(b)(3), a clearing firm with a fail to deliver in a threshold security must close it out after the fail has lasted:',
 '13 consecutive settlement days', ['3 consecutive settlement days', '35 consecutive calendar days', '60 consecutive calendar days'],
 'Rule 203(b)(3) requires a participant with a fail to deliver in a threshold security for 13 consecutive settlement days to close it out by purchasing securities of like kind and quantity, and restricts further short sales until it does.'),
('A clearing firm has a fail to deliver at the clearing agency that resulted from a short sale. Under Regulation SHO Rule 204 it must close out the position by:',
 'Start of trading on the day after the settlement date', ['The end of the third week after the trade date', 'The 35th calendar day after the trade date, at the close', 'Its next monthly FOCUS filing with FINRA'],
 'Rule 204(a) requires a participant with a fail to deliver from a short sale to close it out by borrowing or purchasing by the beginning of regular trading hours on the settlement day following the settlement date.'),
('A fail to deliver that the participant can show resulted from a long sale must be closed out under Rule 204 by:',
 'The start of trading on the third settlement day after settlement', ['The start of regular trading hours on the trade date', 'The end of the settlement date itself', 'The 60th calendar day after the trade date, at the close'],
 'Rule 204(a)(1) gives long sales, and Rule 204(a)(3) bona fide market making, until the beginning of regular trading hours on the third consecutive settlement day following the settlement date.'),
('A customer sells restricted securities under Rule 144 and the shares are not delivered in time. Under Regulation SHO the fail must be closed out by:',
 'The 35th calendar day after the trade date', ['The settlement date itself', 'The 10th business day after the settlement date', 'The 90th calendar day after the trade date'],
 'Rule 204(a)(2) allows a fail from the sale of a security the seller is deemed to own and intends to deliver, such as Rule 144 restricted stock, to be closed out by the beginning of trading on the 35th consecutive calendar day after the trade date.'),
("Under SEC Rule 10b-18's safe harbor for issuer buybacks, the issuer's purchases on a day generally may not exceed:",
 "25% of the stock's average daily trading volume", ['5% of the shares outstanding', '10% of the public float', "50% of the prior day's volume"],
 'Rule 10b-18 gives a safe harbor from manipulation claims if the issuer uses one broker-dealer a day, avoids the opening trade and the final minutes of trading, pays no more than the highest independent bid or last independent trade, and generally buys no more than 25 percent of average daily trading volume.'),
('Regulation SHO Rule 200(g) requires every sell order in an equity security to be marked:',
 'Long, short or short exempt', ['Solicited or unsolicited', 'Market, limit or stop', 'Agency or principal'],
 'Rule 200(g) requires a broker-dealer to mark all sell orders of equity securities long, short or short exempt.'),
('SEC Rule 15c3-5 requires a broker-dealer that gives customers market access to have:',
 'Pre-trade controls that block orders over set limits', ['A trading floor staffed by a principal at all times', 'Approval from the exchange for each order before it is sent', 'A policy of reviewing trades after the month ends'],
 "The Market Access Rule requires risk management controls, under the firm's direct and exclusive control, that prevent orders exceeding pre-set credit or capital thresholds or failing regulatory requirements, with an annual CEO certification."),
("Under the Limit Up-Limit Down plan, if a stock's quote stays at a price band edge in a limit state for 15 seconds without clearing:",
 'Trading in the stock pauses for five minutes', ['Trading in the stock halts for the rest of the day', 'The price band is removed for the rest of the day', 'Only short sales in the stock are halted'],
 'Under the LULD plan, a stock in a limit state that does not exit within 15 seconds enters a five-minute trading pause on the primary listing market.'),
('Market-wide circuit breakers halt trading for the rest of the day when the S&P 500 falls from the prior close by:',
 '20%', ['7%', '10%', '13%'],
 'A Level 3 decline of 20 percent halts trading for the remainder of the day. Level 1 (7 percent) and Level 2 (13 percent) declines before 3:25 p.m. Eastern halt trading for 15 minutes.'),
('If the S&P 500 drops 7% at 11:00 a.m. Eastern time, market-wide circuit breakers:',
 'Halt trading for 15 minutes', ['Halt trading for the rest of the day', 'Have no effect until a 10% decline', 'Halt only short selling for the day'],
 'A Level 1 decline of 7 percent before 3:25 p.m. Eastern halts trading in all stocks for 15 minutes. After 3:25 p.m. a Level 1 or Level 2 decline does not halt trading.'),
("A trader places a large buy order at 3:59 p.m. to push a stock's closing price higher for a month-end valuation. This is:",
 'Marking the close, a form of manipulation', ['Permitted price discovery near the close', "Best execution for the firm's customers", 'A bona fide hedge of a large position'],
 'Entering orders near the close to influence the closing price is manipulation, prohibited by Exchange Act Section 9(a)(2), Rule 10b-5 and FINRA Rules 2020 and 6140.'),
('Buying and selling the same security with no change in beneficial ownership, to make the market look active, is:',
 'A wash trade', ['A riskless principal trade', 'A cross trade', 'An intermarket sweep'],
 'Wash trades involve no change of beneficial ownership. Exchange Act Section 9(a)(1) and FINRA Rule 6140 prohibit them when done to create a false or misleading appearance of trading.'),
('A trader enters large orders on one side of the market with no intent to let them execute, then cancels them after trading on the other side. This is:',
 'Spoofing or layering', ['Marking the open', 'Payment for order flow', 'A stop order'],
 'Placing non-bona fide orders to create a false impression of supply or demand and then cancelling them is spoofing or layering, a manipulative practice firms must surveil for.'),
("Under FINRA Rule 5220, a market maker's published quote is firm, meaning the market maker:",
 'Must trade at its quoted price up to its quoted size', ['May change the price after an order arrives', 'Must fill an order of any size at its quoted price', 'Needs principal approval before each trade'],
 'Rule 5220 bars a member from making an offer to buy or sell at a stated price unless it is prepared to buy or sell at that price and under the conditions stated, and SEC Rule 602 obliges it to trade at its published quote up to its published size.'),
('As amended in 2021, SEC Rule 15c2-11 generally lets a broker-dealer publish a quote for an OTC equity security only if:',
 'Current information about the issuer is public', ['The issuer pays the broker-dealer a quoting fee', 'The stock trades above $5 per share', 'The issuer is listed on a national exchange'],
 'Amended Rule 15c2-11 requires that specified current information about the issuer be publicly available before a broker-dealer initiates or resumes quotations, which ended quoting of many companies with no current public information.'),
('A trader exceeds the position limit in her written trading mandate. Her supervisor should first:',
 "Escalate the breach under the firm's procedures", ['Raise the limit so that the breach disappears', 'Wait to see whether the position becomes profitable', 'Tell the trader to move the excess to another account'],
 "Trader mandates and limits must be enforced under Rules 3110 and 15c3-5. A breach must be escalated and reviewed under the firm's procedures, not cured by changing the limit after the fact."),
('Under the Consolidated Audit Trail rules, a firm must report most reportable events for a trading day to CAT by:',
 '8:00 a.m. Eastern on the next trading day', ['The end of the same trading day', 'Ten seconds after each reportable event', 'The fifth business day after the trade'],
 'FINRA Rule 6830 and the CAT plan require industry members to record and report reportable events to the Central Repository by 8:00 a.m. Eastern time on the trading day after the event.'),
("A representative splits a customer's 2,000-share order into four separate orders to earn four commissions. Rule 5290 calls this:",
 'Prohibited order splitting to raise pay', ['Acceptable working of a large customer order', 'A best execution practice the rule requires', 'Allowed as long as each order is filled'],
 'Rule 5290 prohibits splitting a customer order into multiple smaller orders, or otherwise handling it, for the primary purpose of maximizing execution-related compensation.'),
('A firm receives payment for routing customer orders to a market maker. It must disclose this:',
 'At account opening, yearly, on confirmations and in 606 reports', ["Only to FINRA during the firm's annual audit", 'Only if a customer complains about a fill', 'Only to institutional customers that ask for it'],
 'SEC Rule 10b-10 requires the confirmation to state whether payment for order flow is received, Rule 607 requires disclosure at account opening and annually, and Rule 606 reports detail the amounts.'),
]
